// v0.3-M9 C7 review r2 (security): a `sensitive string` map key is refused wherever a shape
// declaration writes the map: a field, a map nested in a field's type, and a union alias variant.
// Correct behavior: does not compile; each of the three is refused by typeck, never by codegen.
shape Vault { entries: Map<sensitive String, Int> }
shape Ledger { pages: Array<Map<sensitive String, Int>> }
shape Holder = Map<sensitive String, Int> | Int
function entrypoint() -> Nothing {
  print(1)
}
